    "tpb_seq": 1,
    "tpb_book": null,
    "tpb_book_en": "<div>Cateora, Philip R., Graham, John L., Gilly, Mary C., Money, R. Bruce. (2024). International Marketing (19th ed). Dubuque, Iowa: McGraw-Hill<br />\nEducation.</div>\n"
  },
  "readings": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB25130",
    "sub_id": "51988",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpc_seq": 1,
    "tpc_book": null,
    "tpc_book_en": "<div>International Marketing is a deep probe into how marketing has historically developed and what kinds of things we need to pay attention to<br />\nwhen entering foreign markets. Dealing with differing cultures calls for a customized approach.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>This book provides an approach and framework for identifying and analyzing the important cultural and environmental uniqueness of any nation or global region. In this context, the reader will not overlook the impact of crucial cultural issues.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>The text is designed to stimulate curiosity about management practices of companies, large and small, seeking market opportunities outside the home country and to raise the reader&rsquo;s consciousness about the importance of viewing international marketing management strategies from a global perspective.</div>\n"
  },
